       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"WhatsApp Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is WhatsApp automation?\", \"a\": \"WhatsApp automation is software that sends, answers, or routes WhatsApp messages for a business when something happens, instead of a person typing each one. A shipped order can trigger a tracking update, a booking can trigger a reminder, and a question about an order can get its status from your records.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I set up WhatsApp automation?\", \"a\": \"Pick one conversation, connect the business phone number to the WhatsApp API, and get your templates approved. Then describe the trigger, the message, and who takes the hard replies to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder'>AI automation builder</a>. Emergent builds the workflow and its contact database, and you try it with your own opted-in number before customers see it.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is WhatsApp automation free?\", \"a\": \"Partly. The WhatsApp Business app is free to download, and its greeting and away messages handle simple auto-replies. On the WhatsApp Business Platform, Meta charges on a per-message basis for what a business sends. Meta does not charge for messages from users to businesses, and each business number gets 1,000 delivered service messages free per month.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I use WhatsApp automation for messages to my own team?\", \"a\": \"Yes, as long as each teammate has opted in on their own number. Shift reminders and a short check-in after a training course work the same way as customer messages. For the check-in, borrow wording from a set of learning and development survey questions and send one per message. The app Emergent builds saves each answer to a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does the 24-hour window affect WhatsApp automation?\", \"a\": \"It decides what the automation is allowed to send. When a contact messages your business, a 24-hour customer service window starts. After it closes, the business can only send pre-approved template messages. Plan for both cases: replies while the window is open, and templates for anything later, such as a reminder sent days after the last chat.\"}, {\"q\": \"Does WhatsApp automation need opt-in from every contact?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Meta's rules say a business can only send messages to WhatsApp users who have opted in to receiving messages from it. Ask at the point where you collect the number, in words that name WhatsApp, and keep the record. Give opt-in its own checkbox rather than folding it into your terms.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a WhatsApp automation bot run a quiz or a poll?\", \"a\": \"Yes. A WhatsApp automation bot can send a question and score the reply before it sends the next. That suits a trivia night or a quick product poll. Number the options so contacts reply with a digit. A set of game survey questions makes a good warm-up round. Emergent builds the question flow and its scoring from one prompt.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can WhatsApp automation hand a chat over to a person?\", \"a\": \"Yes. You list the topics a person must handle, and the app stops answering those chats and alerts a teammate. Send a short holding reply first, such as a note that a person will answer within the hour. The teammate then answers from the same business number, and the thread stays in one place.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does WhatsApp automation through the API add over the free app?\", \"a\": \"The free app sends greeting messages and away messages, which suit a small shop answering by hand. Through the API, an app can send a message the moment an order ships and answer from your order records. Move to the API once the same questions arrive every day.\"}, {\"q\": \"How can WhatsApp automation ask contacts what they want before a launch?\", \"a\": \"Send a short template to contacts who opted in, then ask two or three questions one message at a time and save each answer on the contact. Ask about timing and price before features. A list of audience survey questions gives you wording to start from. Emergent builds the flow and a live dashboard that counts answers as they arrive.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
